    ]},
    {"start": 27.536, "end": 42.416, "text": "Categorical rules, as this court put it colorfully in Dudenhofer, do not readily divide the plausible sheep from the meritless goats because they are inconsistent with the careful, context-sensitive inquiry that both ERISA and Rule 8 require.", "words": [
