  "captions": [
    {"start": 0.161, "end": 5.281, "lines": ["We will hear argument this morning","in case 25-498, Anderson versus Intel"]},
    {"start": 5.281, "end": 8.401, "lines": ["Corporation Investment Policy Committee."]},
    {"start": 8.401, "end": 9.761, "lines": ["Mr. Wessler."]},
    {"start": 9.761, "end": 12.721, "lines": ["Mr. Chief Justice,","and may it please the Court."]},
    {"start": 12.721, "end": 16.161, "lines": ["ERISA's duty","of prudence is inherently flexible."]},
    {"start": 16.161, "end": 18.881, "lines": ["As a result,","this Court has consistently declined"]},
    {"start": 18.881, "end": 23.201, "lines": ["to inject judicially crafted bright","line rules into a determination"]},
    {"start": 23.201, "end": 27.536, "lines": ["of whether a complaint's allegations","plausibly allege imprudence."]},
    {"start": 27.536, "end": 31.616, "lines": ["Categorical rules, as this court","put it colorfully in Dudenhofer,"]},
    {"start": 31.616, "end": 35.456, "lines": ["do not readily divide the plausible sheep","from the meritless goats"]},
    {"start": 35.456, "end": 38.896, "lines": ["because they are inconsistent","with the careful, context-sensitive"]},
    {"start": 38.896, "end": 42.416, "lines": ["inquiry that both ERISA","and Rule 8 require."]},
    {"start": 42.416, "end": 47.296, "lines": ["The Ninth Circuit's meaningful benchmark","requirement is just such a rule."]},
    {"start": 47.296, "end": 50.176, "lines": ["Under it,","a court first asks whether a complaint's"]},
    {"start": 50.176, "end": 52.72, "lines": ["performance allegations on their own."]},
    {"start": 52.72, "end": 56.16, "lines": ["Can plausibly demonstrate imprudence","by identifying a virtually"]},
    {"start": 56.16, "end": 59.28, "lines": ["indistinguishable fund","that performed better."]},
    {"start": 59.28, "end": 62.88, "lines": ["If the complaint fails","to identify that specific fund,"]},
    {"start": 62.88, "end": 65.36, "lines": ["the performance allegations are discarded."]},
    {"start": 65.36, "end": 68.88, "lines": ["And that is true even if the complaint","relies on benchmarks selected"]},
    {"start": 68.88, "end": 72.64, "lines": ["by the fiduciaries themselves","or comparators identified"]},
    {"start": 72.64, "end": 76.32, "lines": ["by benchmarking experts.","In the respondent's view, this rule"]},
    {"start": 76.32, "end": 80.8, "lines": ["is consistent with the ordinary pleading","framework set forth in Twambly and Iqbal,"]},
    {"start": 80.8, "end": 84.608, "lines": ["but under that framework,","Courts must assess all non-conclusory"]},
    {"start": 84.608, "end": 89.008, "lines": ["allegations together in determining","if a complaint plausibly states a claim."]},
    {"start": 89.008, "end": 90.928, "lines": ["The meaningful benchmark requirement"]},
    {"start": 90.928, "end": 95.248, "lines": ["precludes that assessment. And the Ninth","Circuit's rule isn't even necessary."]},
    {"start": 95.248, "end": 99.968, "lines": ["Everyone agrees that without more,","a complaint merely alleging that one"]},
    {"start": 99.968, "end": 104.368, "lines": ["fund performed better than another","won't survive a motion to dismiss."]},
    {"start": 104.368, "end": 106.048, "lines": ["The ordinary pleading standards,"]},
    {"start": 106.048, "end": 109.608, "lines": ["however, are perfectly capable","of weeding out a truly"]},
    {"start": 110.048, "end": 112.016, "lines": ["meritless claim like that."]},
    {"start": 112.016, "end": 114.896, "lines": ["Ultimately, because the meaningful","benchmark rule is both"]},
    {"start": 114.896, "end": 117.136, "lines": ["out of step with Twombly and Iqbal"]},
    {"start": 117.136, "end": 121.456, "lines": ["and an unnecessary solution in search","of a problem, it should be rejected."]},
    {"start": 121.456, "end": 123.896, "lines": ["I welcome the Court's questions."]},
    {"start": 124.336, "end": 128.096, "lines": ["So are you saying that you can prove"]},
    {"start": 128.096, "end": 133.736, "lines": ["imprudence or demonstrate","it by comparing dissimilar funds?"]},
    {"start": 134.416, "end": 137.184, "lines": ["I mean, that is one way.","That's a complaint."]},
    {"start": 137.184, "end": 138.864, "lines": ["So, how would you do that? Sure."]},
    {"start": 138.864, "end": 143.024, "lines": ["So, it's context-dependent,","and there is no one specific"]},
    {"start": 143.024, "end": 148.624, "lines": ["fund that a complaint needs to identify","to make performance allegations relevant"]},
    {"start": 148.624, "end": 151.264, "lines": ["to support a claim of imprudence."]},
    {"start": 151.264, "end": 155.344, "lines": ["It can run a very wide spectrum","of different ways that the complaint"]},
    {"start": 155.344, "end": 157.904, "lines": ["could use performance allegations"]},
    {"start": 157.904, "end": 161.888, "lines": ["to contribute to the overall plausibility","of a complaint."]},
    {"start": 161.888, "end": 165.488, "lines": ["And the way it would do that is,","it would identify a relevant way"]},
    {"start": 165.488, "end": 167.968, "lines": ["of comparing the performance of one fund"]},
    {"start": 167.968, "end": 173.248, "lines": ["with other potential comparators,","and it would explain why that performance"]},
    {"start": 173.248, "end": 177.408, "lines": ["was relevant to the theory","of breach alleged in a complaint."]},
    {"start": 177.408, "end": 182.768, "lines": ["But what the Ninth Circuit has done here","is it has attempted to predefine the kind"]},
    {"start": 182.768, "end": 185.088, "lines": ["of comparison that will count when"]},
    {"start": 185.088, "end": 188.928, "lines": ["a court. Is asking how the performance","allegations contribute to the market. I"]},
    {"start": 188.928, "end": 192.948, "lines": ["think what the Ninth Circuit is saying","is you can't compare apples and orange"]},
    {"start": 193.248, "end": 199.008, "lines": ["if you have a fund, an equity fund,","that is designed to produce"]},
    {"start": 199.008, "end": 205.208, "lines": ["high returns but riskier returns,","and you can't compare that to a fund that."]}
  ]
}
